# velt-customize — Claude Opus everywhere, maximum effort

When executing any velt-customize work (`/velt-customize-run`, `/velt-customize-fix`, `/velt-customize-clear`, `/velt-customize-memory`, or any dispatch of the `velt-orchestrator`, `velt-planner`, `velt-builder`, or `velt-judge` agents):

- **Every agent runs on `claude-opus-4-8-thinking` (Opus 4.8) with maximum reasoning effort.** No tiering, no fast/slow split, no downgrades — this is a deliberate user directive (quality over speed; the recurring failures were reliability + a missing knowledge base, not model tier).
- **Always Claude.** Never re-route a velt-customize step to a generic subagent with a non-Claude model.
- If `claude-opus-4-8-thinking` is unavailable in this environment, substitute **the nearest available Claude Opus / thinking model** (never Sonnet/Fable as a silent downgrade unless Opus is truly unavailable). If no Claude model is available at all, HALT and tell the user instead of silently switching model families.
